## Summary
The article reveals that 81.7% of integrated care personnel are dual-employed with other jobs, leading to overwhelming workloads. They struggle with additional tasks like civil affairs processing and certificate issuance alongside their core care duties, indicating systemic strain.

## Key Points
- 81.7% of integrated care personnel engage in dual employment with other jobs.
- Workload includes civil affairs processing and certificate issuance, compounding their responsibilities.
- Personnel face challenges balancing integrated care with these additional tasks.


